    "## 4. Multi-Omics Factor Analysis (MOFA)\n",
    "\n",
    "SNF told us about patients. MOFA tells us about **the sources of variation themselves**.\n",
    "\n",
    "MOFA ([Argelaguet *et al.* 2018](https://www.embopress.org/doi/full/10.15252/msb.20178124))\n",
    "is a generalisation of factor analysis to multiple views. It assumes that a modest number\n",
    "of hidden **factors** drive the variation in all layers, and it estimates, for each factor:\n",
    "\n",
    "- a **weight** on every feature — how strongly that protein or metabolite loads on it;\n",
    "- a **score** for every patient — where the patient sits along it;\n",
    "- the **variance explained in each view** — which is the part that makes MOFA a genuine\n",
    "  integration method rather than a PCA with extra steps.\n",
    "\n",
    "That last quantity answers our first question directly:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Pattern | Interpretation |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| a factor explains variance in **both** views | shared biology across layers |\n",
    "| a factor explains variance in **one** view only | layer-specific variation (or a technical artefact of that platform) |\n",
    "\n",
    "Sparsity priors (`spikeslab_weights`, `ard_weights`) push most weights to zero, so each\n",
    "factor ends up associated with a short, interpretable list of features."
   ]
  },
  {
